{
  "answer": "During a combined tracking area updating procedure, the MME may include the newly allocated TMSI in the TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT message. If the TMSI is included, the MME transitions to the EMM-COMMON-PROCEDURE-INITIATED state and starts timer T3450. The MME may also include the Location Area Identification (LAI) in the same message, either with or without the TMSI. Additionally, if the MME does not indicate 'SMS only' in the message, it should allocate a TAI list that does not span more than one location area, subject to operator policies. The UE then stores the received LAI, resets the location update attempt counter, sets its update status to U1 UPDATED, and enters MM IDLE state.",
  "evidence": [
    "Clause 5.5.3.2.4 of 3GPP TS 24.301: 'The TMSI reallocation may be part of the combined tracking area updating procedure. The TMSI allocated is then included in the TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT message together with the location area identification (LAI). In this case the MME shall change to state EMM-COMMON-PROCEDURE-INITIATED and shall start the timer T3450 as described in clause 5.4.1.'",
    'Context [1]: "The LAI may be included in the TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT message without TMSI."',
    'Context [1]: "If the MME does not indicate \"SMS only\" in the TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT message, subject to operator policies the MME should allocate a TAI list that does not span more than one location area"',
    'Context [1]: "The UE, receiving a TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT message, stores the received location area identification, resets the location update attempt counter, sets the update status to U1 UPDATED and enters MM state MM IDLE"'
  ]
